</section>
<section id="S10.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">10.3 </span>Change-Manifest Schema</h3>

<div id="S10.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S10.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each Evolver candidate is accompanied by a change manifest, a structured audit record linking the proposed edit to its evidence, mechanism, expected effect, and attribution signal. The manifest makes every harness modification falsifiable: the Critic checks whether the next round’s trace features match the mechanism and impact the manifest predicted. Table <a href="#S10.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ 10.3 Change-Manifest Schema ‣ 10 Prompts and Harness Defaults ‣ HarnessX: A Composable, Adaptive, and Evolvable Agent Harness Foundry" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> defines the manifest fields, and the schema below specifies their representation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S10.T9" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 9: </span>Change-manifest fields. The manifest is the loop’s evidence ledger:
every shipped edit is falsifiable against the next round’s trace-feature deltas.</figcaption>
<table id="S10.T9.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
